            "Matt.1.3",
            "Matt.1.4",
            "Luke.3.33"
          ],
          "genderAsCurated": "Male",
          "ambiguousAsCurated": true,
          "disambiguationNote": "Ram ((Hebrew: אֲרָם Aram) is a son of Shem, according to the Table of Nations in Genesis 10 of the Hebrew Bible, and the father of Uz, Hul, Gether and Mash or Meshech.[1] The Book of Chronicles lists Aram, Uz, Hul, Gether, and Meshech as descendants of Shem, although without stating explicitly that Aram is the father of the other four.[2] Aram is usually regarded as being the eponymous ancestor of the Aramean people of Northern Mesopotamia and Syria.)",
          "generation": null,
          "absoluteChronology": null,
          "musicalAssignment": null,
          "historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed": false,
          "curatedChronologyNotAdopted": {
            "birthYear": "",
