            "The father of Hadadezer, king of Tobah ( 2 Samuel 8:3 2 Samuel 8:12 ) Nehemiah 10:11 The same, probably, as Beth-rehob ( 2 Samuel 10:6 2 Samuel 10:8 ; Judg. 18:28 ), a place in the north of Palestine ( Numbers 13:21 ). It is now supposed to be represented by the castle of Hunin, south-west of Dan, on the road from Hamath into Coele-Syria. A town of Asher ( Joshua 19:28 ), to the east of Zidon. Another town of Asher ( Joshua 19:30 ), kept possession of by the Canaanites ( Judges 1:31 )."
